# lsan.supp — LeakSanitizer suppressions for fabric-gateway-cpp tests
#
# OpenSSL 3.x (libcrypto) makes a number of one-time, process-lifetime
# allocations — algorithm/method tables, error-string slots, RAND/BN caches,
# ex_data indexes, etc. — that it intentionally never frees. They are created
# lazily on first use of EC_KEY/EVP and are reported as leaks by
# LeakSanitizer at process exit. They are library-internal global state, not
# application leaks.
#
# Every leak observed in this codebase roots in libcrypto (CRYPTO_malloc /
# CRYPTO_realloc) with no frames in fabric/ code, so we suppress them to keep
# sanitizer runs green and let genuine (application-side) leaks stand out.
#
# This only hides OpenSSL-internal allocations. Application OpenSSL objects
# (EC_KEY, EVP_PKEY, X509, ...) are held via RAII (unique_ptr<Impl> with the
# matching *_free), so a real leak there surfaces as a non-libcrypto leak and is
# NOT suppressed here.
leak:CRYPTO_malloc
leak:CRYPTO_realloc
